  "user_impact": "The title attribute is read inconsistently or not at all by many screen readers; sighted users only see it on hover.",
  "technical_impact": "Form element without <label>/aria-label, name derived only from title.",
  "source": "WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1, 3.3.2; technique H65 (title attribute to identify form controls)",
  "applicability": "Rendered text-entry, select, slider and spinbutton fields (native or ARIA) without placeholder.",
  "expectation": "Needs review when the field's name comes only from its title attribute:\nvisible on mouse hover only, not to keyboard or touch users. H65 allows it\nwhen the purpose is clear from the visible context, so never a confirmed\nviolation. A field with a label and a title is not reported; a field with a\nplaceholder is forms/placeholder-as-label's case.",
